    "doc-kit-mac": {
      "install": "on-request",
      "for": "the document kit of an office Mac (docs/OFFICE.md, scripts/office/doc-kit.sh): office-install.sh fetches it per user, with no sudo, into <prefix>/kit/<key> with a link current. LibreOffice draws the pages the AI looks at (server/src/files/office-view.ts, in its own sandbox-exec profile); node runs srt, which runs the AI's build commands (Seatbelt, as the signed-in user: server/src/devenv/srt/system-office.ts) with the Node libraries of scripts/dev-env/srt/node-libs.package-lock.json; CPython carries the document libraries (python doc-kit-mac); the Noto CJK fonts draw Korean, Japanese and Chinese (LibreOffice on a Mac has none of its own; it brings Carlito, Caladea and Liberation itself), linked into each render's profile (MYCEL_KIT_FONTS_DIR, server/src/files/office-profile.ts)",
